// A size field: stretches of the world where a body's size is a function of where it stands. A module library: it
// hands its importers one template and emits no document.
//
// A field is a list of zones. Each zone runs along a path from `from` to `to`, two world points, and holds a body that
// stands inside it: within `reach` metres of the path (a capsule), inside its `box` (an axis-aligned box in world
// metres), or both. A body inside a zone whose foot projects onto the path at progress t (0 at `from`, 1 at `to`, held
// to the path's two ends) is given the size
//
//   start * power(end / start, t)
//
// in its size register every tick: `start` at `from`, `end` at `to`, and the same factor over every equal step between.
// That is the curve a flight of stairs into a small place needs: a body a sixth its size takes steps a sixth as long, so
// each tread costs it the same share of its stride all the way up. A zone's `ease` bends that curve still at both ends:
// the exponent is `sizeFieldEase(t, ease)`, t itself at 0 and smoothstep's 3t^2 - 2t^3 at 1, so a body's size starts and
// stops changing gently instead of at once. A zone's `part` names the share [a, b] of one longer path it covers, so a
// path that turns is one curve written as several zones (`sizeFieldPath`): each zone reads its progress as
// `a + t (b - a)` of the whole before the curve, so a size eased along the whole path stands still only at the path's two
// ends, not at every corner. Such a path turns on circular arcs (paths.puck's `roundedPath`): an `arc` zone reads a
// body's progress by its angle about the arc's centre, so the progress, and the size, run on continuously through the
// turn whichever line a body takes round it, where the nearest point of a bare corner would jump across its inner
// bisector. A vertical path inside a box (from a storey's floor
// to the next one's, over a stair's well or a lift's shaft) sizes a body by its height alone, whatever the stair's
// form, a switchback's flights and a spiral's helix alike. A zone whose `from` and `to` meet (or that names neither)
// gives `start` throughout: a whole floor held at one size.
//
// The first zone, in list order, that holds the body decides its size, so zones may overlap and the earlier wins: a
// stair's well listed before the floor round it sizes a body on the stair by its height and one beside it by the floor.
// Outside every zone the register keeps the size the body last took, so leaving a field at its small end leaves the
// body small until a field (the same one walked back, or another) grows it again.
//
// `passes` names body registers (state.body): a body holding any of them nonzero is given the `passSize` size inside
// every zone instead, so a pass a puzzle grants keeps a body its full size where the field would shrink it.
//
// `sizeHold` is a body register (size-hold.puck, which a world imports beside this) every field reads, for an escape hatch such as a debug noclip: 2 while a source holds
// the body (the source writes it), when every field gives it `passSize` wherever it stands, inside a zone or not; 1 once
// the source lets go, when it keeps that size inside the zones until it stands outside every zone of the field, which
// clears it to 0. So turning the hatch off inside a small place changes nothing until the body walks out.
//
// The size is the body's own register, fixed point, written by a world rule from its live position (bodyPosition), so
// it is world truth: its collider, speeds, step height, jump, engage reach and gravity response follow it on the
// authority (bodies.scale), and every observer, a window or another player or a spectator camera, reads the same
// register and draws the body the size it is. Growth is held to the room about the body
// (WorldBody.SetScaleWithinClearance): a body asked to grow under a low ceiling stays the largest size that fits, and
// grows on once it walks clear.
//
// A field stands in a frame (frame.puck), as the group it sizes does: its zones are written in the group's own
// coordinates and carried into the world by `frame`, and its sizes are the group's, so they are multiplied by the frame's
// scale. A body in a group stood at half size therefore takes half the size the field writes at full size, and its
// collider, speeds, gravity, jump and reach follow (bodies.scale), so moving through the scaled group feels as moving
// through the unscaled one does. A path and a capsule hold at any yaw; a box is the world box about the group's box
// (frameBox), exact at a whole number of quarter turns.
//
// The field's sizes live in a world table, `sizeField-<name>`, keyed by the names `sizes` gives them, so a running World
// is retuned without a reload:
//
//   world.state sizeField-<name>                        reads every named size
//   world.state.cell.set sizeField-<name> <key> <size>  sets one; the field sizes bodies by it from the next tick
//
// or edit the template's arguments and let the watch reload. The sizes are a look and feel, the author's: the standard
// sets no default for them.
//
// sizeField(
//   name:     the field's name; names its rule `size-field-<name>` and its table `sizeField-<name>`
//   zones:    the zones, first match wins, each { from, to, start, end, reach, box, ease, part }, in the frame's
//             coordinates:
//               from, to   the path's two points, [x, y, z] (both omitted: one size throughout)
//               start, end keys of `sizes`: the size at `from` and at `to` (`end` omitted: `start` throughout)
//               reach      how far either side of the path, in metres, the zone holds a body (omitted: no capsule)
//               box        { x0, x1, y0, y1, z0, z1 }, metres, the box the zone holds a body in (omitted: none)
//               ease       0 to 1, how still the curve stands at its ends (omitted: 0, the plain power curve)
//               part       [a, b], the share of a longer path `from` to `to` covers (omitted: [0, 1])
//               arc        { centre, radius, sweep, e1, e2 }: the zone is an arc of a path, not a segment
//                          (paths.puck's arc pieces): it holds a body within `reach` of the arc and reads its
//                          progress as its angle about `centre` from `e1` toward `e2`, over `sweep` radians
//   sizes:    the named sizes, [{ key, value }], each a multiplier of the body's authored size in the frame
//   register: the body register its size lives in; the one bodies.scale names
//   passes:   body registers that, nonzero, give a body `passSize` inside every zone
//   passSize: the key of `sizes` a pass holder takes (omitted: the first size)
//   frame:    the frame the zones and sizes stand in (omitted: the world's own, frameIdentity)
// )

import "frame"
import "paths"


// A zone as the rule reads it: its box and capsule flags, which axes its path moves along, and the path's span and
// squared length, whose quotient with the foot's offset dotted along the span is its progress. Every value here folds
// at expansion.
let sizeFieldNoBox = { x0: 0, x1: 0, y0: 0, y1: 0, z0: 0, z1: 0 }
function sizeFieldZone(frame, zone) = sizeFieldPrepared(sizeFieldPlaced(frame, ({
  from [0, 0, 0]
  to [0, 0, 0]
  reach: 0
  box: sizeFieldNoBox
  end: zone.start
  ease: 0
  part [0, 1]
  arc: null
} with zone)))

// The exponent a progress t in [0, 1] along a path gives its size curve: t itself at `ease` 0, smoothstep's 3t^2 - 2t^3
// at 1 (still at both ends), and the blend between. The field's rule reads it over a body's progress and an importer
// reads it over a point it builds at (size-tunnel.puck), so what is drawn for a size and the size a body takes there
// follow one curve.
function sizeFieldEase(t, ease) = (t + (ease * (((t * t) * (3 - (2 * t))) - t)))
// The size the curve gives at a progress t of the whole path, between the sizes `start` and `end` (numbers).
function sizeFieldAt(start, end, t, ease = 0) = (start * power((end / start), sizeFieldEase(t, ease)))
// The local the rule reads a zone's exponent from: its progress along its own path where the zone is a whole plain
// path, otherwise the local `share{z}` holding that progress carried into the zone's span of the whole path and eased,
// which the rule declares for such a zone alone, so a plain field's rule reads exactly what it read before.
function sizeFieldShareName(zone, z) = (zone.plain ? $"along{z}" : $"share{z}")
// The square of the nearest an arc zone holds a foot to its centre, its radius less its reach (none past the centre).
function sizeFieldInner(zone) = ((zone.arc.radius > zone.reach) ? ((zone.arc.radius - zone.reach) *
  (zone.arc.radius - zone.reach)) : 0)

// The zones that size a body along a rounded path (paths.puck's `roundedPath`) as one curve: a zone a piece, each
// covering its share of the whole length, from the size `start` at the path's first point to `end` at its last (keys of
// `sizes`, the field's named sizes). Each zone holds a body within `reach.base + reach.bySize * size` of its piece, the
// size the larger of its piece's two ends, so a path whose bore grows with its size holds a body only as far out as the
// bore reaches there. The arcs come first, since the first zone that holds a body decides: a line's end reaches round
// its corner, where the arc reads the body's progress truly. So the size runs on continuously everywhere as long as each
// arc's radius is at least its reach and its ends stand further apart than the reach of the lines it joins
// (2 radius sin(sweep / 2) > reach), which the caller chooses the radii to keep.
function sizeFieldPath(pieces, start, end, sizes, reach, ease = 0) = let curve = {
  start: start
  end: end
  from: sizeFieldValue(sizes, start)
  to: sizeFieldValue(sizes, end)
  reach: reach
  ease: ease
  total: roundedPathLength(pieces)
} in
concat(
  map(filter(pieces, p => (p.kind == "arc")), p => sizeFieldPathZone(p, curve)),
  map(filter(pieces, p => (p.kind == "line")), p => sizeFieldPathZone(p, curve))
)
function sizeFieldValue(sizes, key) = find(sizes, s => (s.key == key)).value
function sizeFieldPathZone(p, curve) = let a = (p.start / curve.total) in
let b = ((p.start + p.length) / curve.total) in
{
  from: roundedPieceAt(p, p.start)
  to: roundedPieceAt(p, (p.start + p.length))
  start: curve.start
  end: curve.end
  reach: (curve.reach.base + (curve.reach.bySize * maximum(
    sizeFieldAt(curve.from, curve.to, a, curve.ease),
    sizeFieldAt(curve.from, curve.to, b, curve.ease)
  )))
  ease: curve.ease
  part [a, b]
  arc: ((p.kind == "arc") ? { centre: p.centre, radius: p.radius, sweep: p.sweep, e1: p.e1, e2: p.e2 } : null)
}
// A zone carried from its frame into the world: its path's points (and an arc's centre, radius and axes), its reach and
// its box.
function sizeFieldPlaced(frame, zone) = zone with {
  from: frameAt(frame, zone.from)
  to: frameAt(frame, zone.to)
  reach: frameLength(frame, zone.reach)
  box: ((zone.box.x1 > zone.box.x0) ? frameBox(frame, zone.box) : sizeFieldNoBox)
  arc: ((zone.arc == null) ? null : {
    centre: frameAt(frame, zone.arc.centre)
    radius: frameLength(frame, zone.arc.radius)
    sweep: zone.arc.sweep
    e1: rotatePoint(frameTurn(frame), zone.arc.e1)
    e2: rotatePoint(frameTurn(frame), zone.arc.e2)
  })
}
function sizeFieldPrepared(zone) = sizeFieldFolded(
  zone,
  [(zone.to[0] - zone.from[0]), (zone.to[1] - zone.from[1]), (zone.to[2] - zone.from[2])]
)
function sizeFieldFolded(zone, span) = sizeFieldSpanned(
  zone,
  span,
  ((span[0] * span[0]) + (span[1] * span[1]) + (span[2] * span[2]))
)
function sizeFieldSpanned(zone, span, spanSquared) = zone with {
  span: span
  boxed: (zone.box.x1 > zone.box.x0)
  capsule: (zone.reach > 0)
  ax: ((spanSquared > 0) and (span[0] != 0))
  ay: ((spanSquared > 0) and (span[1] != 0))
  az: ((spanSquared > 0) and (span[2] != 0))
  moving: (spanSquared > 0)
  spanSquared: ((spanSquared > 0) ? spanSquared : 1)
  plain: ((zone.ease == 0) and (zone.part[0] == 0) and (zone.part[1] == 1))
  curved: (zone.arc != null)
}

template sizeField(name, zones, sizes, register = "size", passes = [], passSize = "", frame = frameIdentity) {
  state {
    world {
      row {
        name: $"sizeField-{name}"
        kind: Fixed
        capacity: length(sizes)
        cells: map(sizes, size => { key: size.key, value: (size.value * frame.scale) })
      }
    }
  }

  let prepared = map(zones, zone => sizeFieldZone(frame, zone))
  let count = length(prepared)
  let passKey = ((passSize == "") ? sizes[0].key : passSize)

  rule $"size-field-{name}" {
    local px = bodyPosition(each, x)
    local py = bodyPosition(each, y)
    local pz = bodyPosition(each, z)
    // Whether the body holds a pass: any of the named registers nonzero.
    local held0 = 0
    for (pass, f) in passes {
      local $"held{f + 1}" = (bodyState(each, pass) != 0) or $"held{f}"
    }
    // The zones in order: `size{z}` the size the first of the first z zones that holds the body gives it, 0 while none
    // does (every size is positive). Two locals a plain zone, three an eased one or one covering part of a path, and five
    // an arc, so a field of a dozen pieces of a turning path stays inside a rule's locals.
    local size0 = 0.0
    for (zone, z) in prepared {
      // An arc's progress: the foot's offset from the centre along its two axes, and the angle they make over the arc's
      // sweep, not held to the arc's ends (a foot outside them is outside the zone).
      for e in (zone.curved ? [z] : []) {
        local $"arcA{e}" = (
          ((px - zone.arc.centre[0]) * zone.arc.e1[0]) +
          ((py - zone.arc.centre[1]) * zone.arc.e1[1]) +
          ((pz - zone.arc.centre[2]) * zone.arc.e1[2])
        )
        local $"arcB{e}" = (
          ((px - zone.arc.centre[0]) * zone.arc.e2[0]) +
          ((py - zone.arc.centre[1]) * zone.arc.e2[1]) +
          ((pz - zone.arc.centre[2]) * zone.arc.e2[2])
        )
        local $"along{e}" = arcTangent2($"arcB{e}", $"arcA{e}") / zone.arc.sweep
      }
      // A segment's progress: the foot's progress along the path, held to its two ends. The dot product is divided by the
      // span's squared length here rather than multiplied by a folded reciprocal, so a foot at either end reads exactly 0
      // or 1.
      for e in (zone.curved ? [] : [z]) {
        local $"along{e}" = (
          zone.moving ?
            clamp(
              (
                (zone.ax ? ((px - zone.from[0]) * zone.span[0]) : 0) +
                (zone.ay ? ((py - zone.from[1]) * zone.span[1]) : 0) +
                (zone.az ? ((pz - zone.from[2]) * zone.span[2]) : 0)
              ) / zone.spanSquared,
              0,
              1
            ) :
          0.0
        )
      }
      // A zone eased or covering part of a longer path reads its exponent from its progress carried into its part and
      // eased (sizeFieldShareName); a plain zone declares nothing more.
      for e in (zone.plain ? [] : [z]) {
        local $"share{e}" = sizeFieldEase(
          (zone.part[0] + (clamp($"along{e}", 0, 1) * (zone.part[1] - zone.part[0]))),
          zone.ease
        )
      }
      // An arc holds a foot between its ends, within reach of its circle in its plane and of its plane.
      for e in (zone.curved ? [z] : []) {
        local $"size{e + 1}" = (
          ($"size{e}" != 0) ? $"size{e}" :
          (
            (
              ($"along{e}" >= 0) and
              ($"along{e}" <= 1) and
              ((($"arcA{e}" * $"arcA{e}") + ($"arcB{e}" * $"arcB{e}")) >= sizeFieldInner(zone)) and
              (
                (($"arcA{e}" * $"arcA{e}") + ($"arcB{e}" * $"arcB{e}")) <=
                  ((zone.arc.radius + zone.reach) * (zone.arc.radius + zone.reach))
              ) and
              (
                (
                  ((px - zone.arc.centre[0]) * (px - zone.arc.centre[0])) +
                  ((py - zone.arc.centre[1]) * (py - zone.arc.centre[1])) +
                  ((pz - zone.arc.centre[2]) * (pz - zone.arc.centre[2]))
                ) -
                  (($"arcA{e}" * $"arcA{e}") + ($"arcB{e}" * $"arcB{e}"))
              ) <=
                (zone.reach * zone.reach)
            ) ?
              (
                $"sizeField-{name}"[zone.start] *
                power($"sizeField-{name}"[zone.end] / $"sizeField-{name}"[zone.start], $"share{e}")
              ) :
            0.0
          )
        )
      }
      // A segment holds a foot inside its box, and within reach of the path's nearest point: a capsule, so a body
      // stepping off either end within reach takes that end's size exactly.
      for e in (zone.curved ? [] : [z]) {
        local $"size{e + 1}" = (
          ($"size{e}" != 0) ? $"size{e}" :
          (
            (
              (
                zone.boxed ?
                  (
                    (px >= zone.box.x0) and
                    (px <= zone.box.x1) and
                    (py >= zone.box.y0) and
                    (py <= zone.box.y1) and
                    (pz >= zone.box.z0) and
                    (pz <= zone.box.z1)
                  ) :
                1
              ) and
              (
                zone.capsule ?
                    (
                      (
                        (
                          (px - zone.from[0] - ($"along{e}" * zone.span[0])) *
                          (px - zone.from[0] - ($"along{e}" * zone.span[0]))
                        ) +
                        (
                          (py - zone.from[1] - ($"along{e}" * zone.span[1])) *
                          (py - zone.from[1] - ($"along{e}" * zone.span[1]))
                        ) +
                        (
                          (pz - zone.from[2] - ($"along{e}" * zone.span[2])) *
                          (pz - zone.from[2] - ($"along{e}" * zone.span[2]))
                        )
                      ) <=
                      (zone.reach * zone.reach)
                    ) :
                  1
              )
            ) ?
              (
                $"sizeField-{name}"[zone.start] *
                power($"sizeField-{name}"[zone.end] / $"sizeField-{name}"[zone.start], $"{sizeFieldShareName(zone, e)}")
              ) :
            0.0
          )
        )
      }
    }
    local hold = bodyState(each, sizeHold)
    local inside = $"size{count}" != 0
    local target = ($"held{length(passes)}" or (hold != 0)) ? $"sizeField-{name}"[passKey] : $"size{count}"
    local holdNext = ((hold == 1) and not inside) ? 0.0 : hold
    when ((inside or hold) and bodyState(each, register) != target) or hold != holdNext
    mode: Level
    forEach: $players
    if (inside or hold) and bodyState(each, register) != target {
      setBodyState(key: $each, state: register, expression: target)
    }
    if hold != holdNext {
      setBodyState(key: $each, state: "sizeHold", expression: holdNext)
    }
  }
}
